See SCEWEVCFG0 for description.</description>
          <access>read-write</access>
          <fields>
            <field>
              <name>RESERVED8</name>
              <description>[31:8] Software should not rely on the value of a reserved. Writing any other value than the reset value may result in undefined behavior.</description>
              <bitWidth>24</bitWidth>
              <bitOffset>8</bitOffset>
              <access>read-only</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>EV0_POL</name>
              <description>[7:7] Polarity of SCEWEVCFG0.EV0_SEL event.

When SCEWEVCFG0.COMB_EV_EN is 0:

0: Non-inverted.
1: Non-inverted.

When SCEWEVCFG0.COMB_EV_EN is 1.

0: Non-inverted.
1: Inverted.</description>
              <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
              <bitOffset>7</bitOffset>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>EV1_POL</name>
              <description>[6:6] Polarity of EV1_SEL event.

When SCEWEVCFG0.COMB_EV_EN is 0:

0: Non-inverted.
1: Non-inverted.

When SCEWEVCFG0.COMB_EV_EN is 1.

0: Non-inverted.
1: Inverted.</description>
              <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
              <bitOffset>6</bitOffset>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>EV1_SEL</name>
              <description>[5:0] Select the event source from the synchronous event bus to be used in event equation.</description>
