    <peripheral>
      <name>AUX_TIMER01</name>
      <baseAddress>0x400C7000</baseAddress>
      <addressBlock>
        <offset>0</offset>
        <size>0x1000</size>
        <usage>registers</usage>
      </addressBlock>
      <description>AUX Timer 0 and AUX Timer 1 (AUX_TIMER01) are two 16-bit timers capable of generating one event each:
- AUX_EVCTL:EVSTAT3.AUX_TIMER0_EV.
- AUX_EVCTL:EVSTAT3.AUX_TIMER1_EV.

The events are described in T0TARGET and T1TARGET. Subscribers to the AUX event bus can use these events to sequence and trigger actions.

AUX_SYSIF:PEROPRATE.TIMER01_OP_RATE sets the peripheral clock frequency used by the prescaler, timer, and event logic to SCE or AUX bus rate. To use AUX_TIMER01:
- AUX_SCE must set AUX_SYSIF:PEROPRATE.TIMER01_OP_RATE to SCE_RATE.
- System CPU must set AUX_SYSIF:PEROPRATE.TIMER01_OP_RATE to BUS_RATE.
- The timers must only subscribe to events updated at the peripheral clock frequency or lower.

Unexpected execution behavior can result if software does not obey these rules.</description>
      <registers>
        <register>
          <name>T0CFG</name>
          <addressOffset>0x0</addressOffset>
          <size>32</size>
          <description>Timer 0 Configuration</description>
          <access>read-write</access>
          <fields>
            <field>
              <name>RESERVED15</name>
              <description>[31:15] Software should not rely on the value of a reserved. Writing any other value than the reset value may result in undefined behavior.</description>
              <bitWidth>17</bitWidth>
              <bitOffset>15</bitOffset>
              <access>read-only</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>TICK_SRC_POL</name>
              <description>[14:14] Tick source polarity for Timer 0.</description>
              <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
              <bitOffset>14</bitOffset>
              <access>read-write</access>
              <enumeratedValues>
                <enumeratedValue>
                  <name>FALL</name>
                  <value>1</value>
                  <description>Count on falling edges of TICK_SRC.</description>
                </enumeratedValue>
                <enumeratedValue>
                  <name>RISE</name>
                  <value>0</value>
                  <description>Count on rising edges of TICK_SRC.</description>
                </enumeratedValue>
              </enumeratedValues>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>TICK_SRC</name>
              <description>[13:8] Select Timer 0 tick source from the synchronous event bus.</description>
              <bitWidth>6</bitWidth>
              <bitOffset>8</bitOffset>
              <access>read-write</access>
